Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||09-13-2000||01:19 PM||||Hi, <BR>I picked up a leather e-brake handle off of a grand am gt (not the whole lever, just the handle part on the end) and am looking to install it on my fiero's e-brake lever.  The dimensions of the two handles are the same, but I can't seem to get the Fiero handle off of the car.  The Grand Am one had a single phillips head screw holding it on.  Is the Fiero one glued?  Any ideas on removing it?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Michael Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||286SE'S||09-13-2000||03:16 PM||||They don't come off. Might be glued, but seem to be molded to the metal. If you are SURE the new one would fit, bust the old one off with some vice grips they aren't very strong.<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
